# Project stack and Svelte MCP workflow

## Stack (for agents)

- **Language:** TypeScript  
- **Package manager:** npm  
- **Common commands:** `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm run test`  
- **Tooling:** ESLint, Prettier, Vitest, `@sveltejs/adapter-netlify` (see [ADR-006](adrs/ADR-006-serverless-and-secret-boundary.md) for portability vs configured adapter)

Architecture and boundaries are defined in **`adrs/INDEX.md`** (Accepted ADRs only) and **`adrs/GOVERNANCE.md`**.

## Svelte MCP server

When the task involves **Svelte or SvelteKit** (components, runes, routes, loads, SSR), use the **Svelte MCP** tools in this order:

### 1. `list-sections`

Call **first** to discover documentation sections (titles, `use_cases`, paths).

### 2. `get-documentation`

After choosing relevant sections from `list-sections`, fetch **all** sections needed for the task. Use `use_cases` to decide scope.

### 3. `svelte-autofixer`

Run on **Svelte code you author or edit**. **Repeat** until it reports no issues or suggestions.

### 4. `playground-link`

Only after the user **confirms** they want a playground link. **Do not** call if code was written into this repository’s files (use local files instead).

---

Svelte **runes, UI, accessibility, and bits-ui / Tailwind** conventions live in [`.cursor/rules/svelte-5-ui-conventions.mdc`](./svelte-5-ui-conventions.mdc). Remaining `agents.md` content is being distributed per [`docs/adr-and-rules-todo.md`](docs/adr-and-rules-todo.md). Human contributors can rely on **`README.md`**, **`adrs/INDEX.md`**, and `.cursor/rules/` for entrypoints.
